# Overall exposure ceiling for repro-daemon-worker.service, in tenths:
# `26` means 2.6. It is the measured value of the unit ALONE, analysed by the
# pinned systemd-analyze 260.1 under a private `--root` that holds nothing but
# the rendered unit, so it is the same number on every host. Measured
# 2026-11-12 at reprobuild e995221fb on nixos-ci-bare-002 (bare metal), both
# as-is and with LXC's drop-in on the analyzer's unit search path.
#
# This file once recorded a ceiling per host class (`none = 26`,
# `virtualized = 31`). The 0.5 was not the analyzer failing to verify checks
# inside a container: `systemd-analyze security --offline` without `--root`
# loads the HOST's unit directories and applies the drop-ins it finds there
# before scoring. LXC's generator writes
# /run/systemd/system/service.d/zzz-lxc-service.conf into every container
# (https://github.com/lxc/distrobuilder/blob/main/distrobuilder/lxc.generator),
# turning off ProtectControlGroups, ProtectKernelTunables, ProtectProc and
# ProcSubset for every service. With that drop-in on the search path, the
# analysis prints 3.1 and the same last 25 rows as GARM run 41251151966. A
# Docker host has no such drop-in and measured 2.6. reprobuild-pm issue
# 2026-11-05-conf-4s-virtualized-class-holds-hosts-that-measure-2-6.
26
